      "labelSegment": 1,
      "labelDy": 12
    }
  ],
  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Codes never in JWTs",
      "items": [
        "6-digit codes are single-use, capped at 5 wrong guesses (hmac.compare_digest), and expire in 24h; resets run 30m with a 3-per-5-min email rate limit",
        "re-signup of an unverified email re-issues a code; verified email answers 409",
        "password reset revokes all sessions; it does not auto-verify the email"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Gates",
      "items": [
        "password verifies first — one constant 401; an unknown email is verified against a fixed dummy hash so both branches take the same time",
        "state gates run only after the password verifies (anti-enumeration by design): blocked → inactive → unverified, each a stable 403",
        "argon2id hashing with an optional concatenated pepper (<APP>_PASSWORD_PEPPER) that lives in env config, never in the DB"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Tokens",
      "items": [
        "access JWT HS256 15m: sub · email · role · iss · iat · exp",
        "refresh is a 128-hex-char opaque token rotated in place; a replayed token misses the WHERE refresh_token CAS (0 rows) → 401 AUTH_INVALID_TOKEN"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
